哎呀呀  零件还真多呀
Boy, oh, boy, that's a lot of pieces.

181
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:53,130
你都知道是干嘛的  对吧
You know what they all do, right?

182
00:07:53,130 --> 00:07:55,180
当然  那还用说
Yes, of course.

183
00:07:55,730 --> 00:07:57,010
那这个是干嘛的
What about this one?

184
00:07:57,010 --> 00:07:59,530
这个嘛...你熟不熟
Well, I... how familiar are you

185
00:07:59,530 --> 00:08:02,230
小型集成逻辑电路呢
with miniaturized integrated logic circuits?

186
00:08:02,230 --> 00:08:02,990
不太熟
Not very.

187
00:08:02,990 --> 00:08:06,040
那你手里拿着的正是这玩意
That right there is a miniaturized integrated logic circuit.

188
00:08:09,170 --> 00:08:10,750
那你能修好它吗
So, can you get it working?

189
00:08:10,750 --> 00:08:13,160
我可是麻省理工毕业的工程师
I'm an MIT-trained engineer.

190
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:16,220
我还为太空站出过一份力呢
I've built components for the space station.

191
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:19,500
我还以为那个零重力厕所不能用呢
I thought the zero-gravity toilet didn't work.

192
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:21,280
能用好吗
It worked fine,

193
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:24,100
只不过设计不适合俄罗斯宇航员
it just wasn't designed for Russian cosmonauts

194
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:27,310
以及他们的全是马铃薯的饮食
and their potato-based diet.

195
00:08:27,310 --> 00:08:28,560
你好啊
Hey, guys.

196
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:29,600
你来啦
Hello.

197
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:31,770
我得把直升飞机退了  我爸...
I have to return the helicopter. My father...

198
00:08:31,770 --> 00:08:34,600
你俩干了什么好事
What did you do?!

199
00:08:36,310 --> 00:08:37,300
别担心
Well, don't worry.

200
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:38,900
他是麻省理工毕业的
He went to MIT.

201
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:40,650
他可以解决任何问题
He can solve any problem,

202
00:08:40,650 --> 00:08:44,730
只要不是来自俄罗斯人的结肠就行
as long as it doesn't originate in a Russian man's colon.

203
00:08:50,390 --> 00:08:51,700
真他妈不敢相信
I don't freaking believe this!

204
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:53,280
别紧张  能装回去
Relax, it'll be fine.

205
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:55,500
不是  你现在必须装回去
No, you have to put this back together right now,

206
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:56,750
我才能拿去退
so I can return it!

207
00:08:56,750 --> 00:08:58,390
你退不了了
You can't return it.

208
00:08:58,390 --> 00:09:01,420
霍华德用保修卡擦屁股了
Howard wiped his bottom with the warranty.

209
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,080
什么
What?!

210
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:05,790
我猜他可能只是打个比方
I think metaphorically.

211
00:09:05,790 --> 00:09:08,860
但他刚真进了厕所好一会呢
But he was in the bathroom for a while.

212
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:11,440
霍华德  我爸不给我零用钱花了
Howard, my father cut me off.

213
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:12,850
我得把这玩意退了  把钱拿回来
I have to get my money back for this!

214
00:09:12,850 --> 00:09:14,060
冷静
Calm down.

215
00:09:14,060 --> 00:09:14,980
好吧
Okay.

216
00:09:15,380 --> 00:09:17,040
好吧  你是对的
Okay, you're right.

217
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:18,930
我是时候站出来
It's time for me to step up

218
00:09:18,930 --> 00:09:21,310
为自己的人生负责了
and take responsibility for my life.

219
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:23,400
当个爷们
Be a man.

220
00:09:25,330 --> 00:09:27,570
妈咪是我啊
Hello, Mummy.

221
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:29,800
拉杰什呀
Hello, Rajesh.

222
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:31,450
这通电话真让我惊喜
What a nice surprise.

223
00:09:31,450 --> 00:09:33,230
我一直很想你
Well, I've been thinking about you.

224
00:09:33,230 --> 00:09:36,060
你好吗  你快乐吗  妈咪
How are you doing? Are you happy, Mummy?

225
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:38,830
乖儿子  真关心我
Such a sweet boy for asking.

226
00:09:38,830 --> 00:09:42,700
真不敢相信你是来自你父亲的毒种
Can't believe you come from the poison seed of your father.

227
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:45,380
我觉得我比较随你
Well, I like to think I take mostly after you.

228
00:09:45,380 --> 00:09:46,570
对了  说起爸爸
Anyway, speaking of Daddy,

229
00:09:46,570 --> 00:09:48,990
我们刚进行了一次非常奇怪的通话
I had a very strange conversation with him.

230
00:09:48,990 --> 00:09:51,100
他说以后没钱打生活费给我了
He said he couldn't afford to send me money anymore

231
00:09:51,100 --> 00:09:54,050
因为他有活跃的社交生活
because of his active social life.

232
00:09:54,050 --> 00:09:57,240
这话什么意思  "活跃的社交生活"
What does that mean, "active social life"?

233
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:59,150
好啦  咱们别聊他了
Well, let's not talk about him

234
00:09:59,150 --> 00:10:01,480
谁在乎他有没有在密谋什么诡计啊
or whatever shenanigans he may or may not be up to.

235
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:03,010
咱们来聊聊你吧
Let's talk about you.

236
00:10:03,890 --> 00:10:06,370
拉杰什  你爸是不是跟人约会了
Rajesh, is your father seeing someone?

237
00:10:06,370 --> 00:10:09,470
妈咪  我只知道他是一个单身多金的医生
All I know, Mummy, is that he's a single wealthy doctor,

238
00:10:09,470 --> 00:10:10,900
而现在出于某种原因
and now, for some reason,

239
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:14,300
突然没钱给你的宝贝儿子了
there's no money for your little boy.

240
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:18,620
好  不管你老爸之前给你多少钱
Well, however much money your father was giving you,

241
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:19,650
我给你更多
I'll give you more.

242
00:10:19,650 --> 00:10:21,800
谢谢妈咪  我爱你
Thank you, Mummy, I love you!

243
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:24,890
一人一台直升机
Helicopters for everybody!

244
00:10:26,430 --> 00:10:27,900
怎么这么久啊
What's taking so long?

245
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:29,890
我觉得这么穿不行
I don't think this is gonna work.

246
00:10:29,890 --> 00:10:31,880
出来给我看看
Just let me see.

247
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:39,340
亲爱的  毕业长袍里
Sweetie, you know you're supposed to wear clothes

248
00:10:39,340 --> 00:10:41,240
应该穿上衣服
underneath a graduation gown.

249
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:44,040
首先  我很惊讶你知道这点
A: surprised you know that.

250
00:10:44,370 --> 00:10:48,100
其次  我想让你觉得我是一个性感毕业生
B: I wanted to look like a sexy graduate for you.

251
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:49,520
你成功了
Well, you do.

252
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:52,080
-谢谢  -好啦
- Thank you. - Yeah.

253
00:10:52,950 --> 00:10:55,220
反正你是视频语聊  他们也看不到你的腿
You're gonna be on Skype; they're not gonna see your legs.

254
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:57,420
以防万一  我还是穿上裤子吧
Well, I'm gonna go put on some pants just in case.

255
00:10:57,420 --> 00:11:01,340
但我要说一句  这样穿真的好"解放"
But I have to say, this is very freeing.

256
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:05,420
系条腰带  我就带你去个好地方
Add a belt and I'll take you someplace nice.

257
00:11:06,230 --> 00:11:09,010
没问题
Done and done.

258
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:17,030
好了  我已经把故障缩小到
Okay, I think I've narrowed it down

259
00:11:17,030 --> 00:11:20,790
飞机通讯芯片上一个错误的针脚
to a faulty pin on the onboard communication chip.

260
00:11:20,790 --> 00:11:23,050
真厉害
Very impressive.

261
00:11:23,050 --> 00:11:25,300
等你修完那台
You know, when you're done with that,

262
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:28,140
可以看下这台吗
can you look at this?

263
00:11:29,290 --> 00:11:31,890
它不会冒烟了
It doesn't make smoke anymore.

264
00:11:31,890 --> 00:11:33,680
一个个来
One toy at a time.

265
00:11:33,680 --> 00:11:34,880
抱歉
Mm. Sorry.

266
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:36,640
或许这样最好
Ah, maybe it's for the best.

267
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:38,450
我听说火车头的烟
I hear locomotive smoke

268
00:11:38,450 --> 00:11:42,150
是火车宅们第二大死因
is the second leading cause of death among train aficionados.

269
00:11:42,730 --> 00:11:43,920
第一大死因是什么
What's the first one?

270
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:45,750
自杀
Suicide.

271
00:11:46,650 --> 00:11:47,850
错
Wrong.

272
00:11:47,850 --> 00:11:50,180
肥胖
Obesity.

273
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:53,040
我把你要的工具拿来了
I have the tool you wanted.

274
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:54,430
谢谢
Thank you.

275
00:11:54,430 --> 00:11:56,270
你们其实不必这么费劲
You guys don't have to go to the trouble.

276
00:11:56,270 --> 00:11:57,250
哥现在又有钱了
I'm back in the money now;

277
00:11:57,250 --> 00:11:59,170
再买一台就好啦
I can just buy another helicopter.

278
00:11:59,170 --> 00:12:00,220
重点不是钱
It's not about the money.

279
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:01,620
而是解决问题
It's about solving a problem.

280
00:12:01,620 --> 00:12:03,200
这是我当工程师的初衷
It's why I became an engineer.

281
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:05,750
我喜欢做这个  我学的也是这个
It's what I like to do, it's what I'm trained to do.

282
00:12:05,750 --> 00:12:06,880
这就是我
It's who I am.

283
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:11,460
瞧你  小工程师做到了
Oh, look at you-- the little engineer that could.

284
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:11,460
源自童书《小引擎做到了》

285
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:14,100
为什么不找技术支持呢
Why don't you just call tech support?

286
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:16,980
-说啥呢  -太逊了
- Hey! - Not cool!

287
00:12:16,980 --> 00:12:17,740
怎么了
What?

288
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:19,510
这个世上有两种人
There's two kinds of people in this world:

289
00:12:19,510 --> 00:12:20,980
打给技术支持求助的人
those who call tech support

290
00:12:20,980 --> 00:12:24,310
与嘲笑前者的那种人
and those who make fun of the people who call tech support.

291
00:12:24,310 --> 00:12:26,150
我就每次都打给技术支持啊
I call tech support all the time.

292
00:12:26,150 --> 00:12:28,640
-你居然找技术支持  -真没用
- You call tech support! - What a baby!

293
00:12:30,450 --> 00:12:33,210
现在  我们的毕业典礼演讲
And now, for our commencement address,

294
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:35,900
邀请到了我们最杰出的校友之一
one of our most distinguished alumni,

295
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:41,050
加州理工名物理学家莱纳德·霍夫斯塔德
noted Caltech physicist Dr. Leonard Hofstadter.

296
00:12:44,620 --> 00:12:46,840
各位教员  各位同学
Members of the faculty, students,

297
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:49,420
我今天很高兴能为大家致辞
I'm excited to speak to you today.

298
00:12:49,420 --> 00:12:52,620
我脑海中一直想起上次来这礼堂的情景
I can't help but remember the last time I was in this auditorium.

299
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:54,310
两个长曲棍球队的人
Two guys from the lacrosse team

300
00:12:54,310 --> 00:12:57,340
拿我的气喘药吸入器当球打  不让我接
played keep-away with my asthma inhaler.

301
00:12:57,340 --> 00:13:01,180
我毕业十年同学会的事就不讲了
But enough about my ten-year reunion.

302
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:03,740
我也想再花点时间
I'd also like to take a moment

303
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:05,820
感谢我美丽的未婚妻
to thank my beautiful fiancee

304
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:07,280
即使在天气不允许的情况下
for to helping make this speech possible,

305
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:10,160
仍将不可能变成现实
even though weather nearly prevented it.

306
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:11,910
大家好啊
Oh. Hello.

307
00:13:11,910 --> 00:13:13,550
我不知道他会把镜头转过来
I-I didn't know he was gonna point it at me,

308
00:13:13,550 --> 00:13:14,750
所以...
so...

309
00:13:14,750 --> 00:13:16,580
别吸毒  别辍学哦
don't do drugs and stay in school.

310
00:13:16,580 --> 00:13:17,580
他们要毕业了
They're graduating.

311
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:19,670
好吧  再见
Okay, bye!

312
00:13:21,870 --> 00:13:23,720
好了  电源供给重新连接上了
All right, the power supply is reconnected.

313
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:24,850
我觉得我们能出征啦
I think we're back in business.

314
00:13:24,850 --> 00:13:27,760
在出征前  先做几个测试
Let's just run a few tests before we take it outside.

315
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:28,850
谢尔顿  网连上了吗
Sheldon, we got WiFi?

316
00:13:28,850 --> 00:13:29,510
已连上
Check.

317
00:13:29,510 --> 00:13:30,110
全球定位系统呢
GPS?

318
00:13:30,110 --> 00:13:30,770
已定位
Check.

319
00:13:30,770 --> 00:13:31,690
电池充满了吗
Battery charged?

320
00:13:31,690 --> 00:13:32,360
已充满
Check.

321
00:13:32,360 --> 00:13:36,070
四小时的生命浪费掉了吗  已浪费
Four hours of our lives gone? Check.

322
00:13:36,790 --> 00:13:38,230
好的  各系统准备工作就绪
All right. All systems go.

323
00:13:38,230 --> 00:13:39,560
倒数五秒
In five...

324
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:43,060
四  三  二  一
...four, three, two, one.

325
00:13:47,620 --> 00:13:50,550
我的小火车以前也能这样
That's what my train used to do.

326
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:55,330
准备好打给技术支持了吗
Ready to call tech support?

327
00:13:55,870 --> 00:13:57,770
电话给我
Give me the number.

328
00:13:58,890 --> 00:14:02,640
打了估计也是某个咖喱国的客服
Probably wind up talking to some foreign guy

329
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:05,770
看着同样的说明书机械化地回答问题
who's reading from the same manual I have.

330
00:14:14,180 --> 00:14:17,050
我爸打来了  都怪你们俩混蛋
It's my father, you jerks.

331
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:21,160
爸比  怎么了
Hello, Daddy.

332
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:22,600
你跟你妈妈说了什么
What did you say to your mother?

333
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:23,330
没有啊
Nothing.

334
00:14:23,330 --> 00:14:25,110
我就打给她问个好
I was just calling to check in,

335
00:14:25,110 --> 00:14:26,560
看看她最近怎么样啊
make sure she's doing okay.

336
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:27,720
她跟你说完电话后
Well, after talking to you,

337
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:30,760
她貌似觉得我是个风流浪子
she seems to think I'm some sort of playboy.

338
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:32,200
真的吗
Really?

339
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:35,240
我不知道她怎么会产生这种想法
I don't know where she'd get an idea like that.

340
00:14:35,650 --> 00:14:38,230
你也懂妈咪这人  还有她常会乱想
You know mummy and her crazy imagination.

341
00:14:38,230 --> 00:14:41,150
我觉得我能随你真是太幸运了
I'm so lucky I take after you.

342
00:14:41,950 --> 00:14:44,380
你觉得你是随我吗
You think you take after me?

343
00:14:44,870 --> 00:14:46,270
我尽量这么想啊
Well, I try to.

344
00:14:46,270 --> 00:14:47,980
如果不是有你做榜样
I certainly wouldn't be a scientist

345
00:14:47,980 --> 00:14:51,370
我也不会去当科学家
if you hadn't been my role model.

346
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:57,890
谁想坐真的直升飞机去拉斯维加斯
Who wants to go to Vegas in a real helicopter?!

347
00:14:59,570 --> 00:15:01,730
弗兰克·鲍姆曾说过
It was L. Frank Baum who said,

348
00:15:01,730 --> 00:15:06,590
"多厉害的小偷  都无法偷走别人脑中的知识
"No thief, however skillful, can rob one of knowledge,

349
00:15:06,590 --> 00:15:11,700
所以知识是最棒最安全的宝藏"
and that is why knowledge is the best and safest treasure."

350
00:15:11,700 --> 00:15:15,650
我自己听了都觉得无聊
Wow, I'm boring myself.

351
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:19,970
抱歉  我现在看不到你们的表情
Sorry, I can't see any of your faces right now,

352
00:15:19,970 --> 00:15:22,470
但我猜大概是这样
but I bet they look like this.

353
00:15:25,510 --> 00:15:29,750
其实  我写了整篇致辞
Uh, you know, I-I wrote an entire speech

354
00:15:29,750 --> 00:15:32,430
要说高中让你准备好面对未来
to say how high school prepares you

355
00:15:32,430 --> 00:15:34,940
以及高中有多美好
and what a wonderful place it is,

356
00:15:34,940 --> 00:15:37,300
但其实我超讨厌高中
but I hated it.

357
00:15:37,300 --> 00:15:41,260
或许有人高中过得很开心  前提是你长这样...
Maybe high school's great if you look like this...

358
00:15:42,690 --> 00:15:47,400
但其实我当年觉得自己超没存在感
...but I didn't even feel like I existed at that school.

359
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:49,570
现在我仔细一想
And now that I think about it,

360
00:15:49,570 --> 00:15:51,800
我猜你们很多人也有这种感觉
I bet a lot of you feel the same way.

361
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:56,340
所以我接下来的致辞
So, for the remainder of my speech,

362
00:15:56,340 --> 00:15:59,030
要献给没有存在感的孩子们
